9. Nc3 O-O 10. Be3 f5 $5 ( 10... Bg4 { is much more popular, but I think this continuation is at least as promising for Black. Our idea is to simply push ...f4 and if White takes en passant he exchanges his strong e5 pawn. } ) 
11. g3 { The critical move, playing for a strategic advantage: I propose a strong pawn sacrifice which has not been tried over the board yet: } Ba5 { It's useful to pin the knight with a tempo first. } 12. Rc1 f4 $1 { We are sacrificing a pawn but just have a look at how our light squared bishop comes into the action. } ( 12... Ne7 13. Bf4 Ng6 { should be also fine. } ) 
13. Bxf4 { This is highly dangerous for White. } Bh3 ( { Just exploiting the holes. Also } 13... Bg4 { is not bad. } ) 
14. Bf1 Qd7 { Black has a serious initiative. White's king is stuck in the middle. } 
